pack aurekai-session-reuse-census
generation control-1
provenance executable-owner census for the 2026-08-27 maturity session, written in the estate's own binding grammar
authority measured
note Written to match fleming-equity-group/reuse-census.yaff rather than invent a sixth pack shape. Every domain need this session touched names its executable_owner and a verification_state. Where I built something the estate already owned, the binding says so and the estate wins.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FINANCIAL MEMBRANE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

binding session:model-rate-discovery
  domain_need price any model the organisation uses, without a human lookup per model
  executable_owner financial_metabolism PriceEvidence / value_provider_usage; rates DERIVED from OpenAI /organization/costs divided by /organization/usage
  estate_role supply the arithmetic and the basis, not a second ledger
  evidence 5 models priced; gpt-5 $1.250 vs published $1.250, gpt-5.4 $2.500 vs $2.500, gpt-4o-mini $0.155 vs $0.150 -- three exact agreements
  evidence gpt-5.6-sol derives 1.91x list and gpt-4.1-mini 1.40x, which is contract pricing a published book cannot show
  verification_state VERIFIED_BY_MEASUREMENT

binding session:sibling-pricing
  domain_need price a model absent from every book
  executable_owner REFUSED -- no owner
  evidence leave-one-out over 389 published models: median error 59%, 2.0x off, only 61.7% within 2x; worst gpt-oss-20b true $0.030 estimated $2.000 (67x)
  estate_role rungs 1 (derived from billing) and 2 (published book) cover every real case
  verification_state KNOWN_GAP

binding session:spend-governance
  domain_need a budget that depletes and carries authority, replacing a constant
  executable_owner financial_metabolism.record_funding_route / choose_funding; resource_admission.decide for concurrent spenders; economic_graphs.record_commitment for expiry
  estate_role supersede BONFYRE_RESOURCE_MAX_DAILY_SPEND_USD, which is declared twice with different values and read by nothing
  defect choose_funding is currency-scoped not provider-scoped; it funded an OpenRouter request from route:compute/anthropic
  verification_state VERIFIED_BY_MEASUREMENT

binding session:native-cost-routing
  domain_need route work to the cheapest adequate model
  executable_owner bonfyre-economy (legacy) / AkaiEconomy (current) -- 'cost-aware routing and budget enforcement'
  estate_role I hand-rolled a funding preflight before finding this. The native router, given the derived rates through its own 'cost record' verb, independently returns fasttext-local as cheapest within budget.
  verification_state OWNER_REUSE_REQUIRED

binding session:usage-metering
  domain_need meter work and produce an invoice
  executable_owner bonfyre-meter / AkaiMeter -- record, usage, invoice, top
  estate_role I hand-rolled token metering. The native meter accepts key/op/bytes/duration and rolls up.
  verification_state OWNER_REUSE_REQUIRED

