binding session:artifact-collapse
  domain_need find and fold equivalent artifact families
  executable_owner bonfyre-index / AkaiIndex -- reuse, equivalence, collapse-preview, collapse-plan, collapse-ledger, confidence-preview
  estate_role I hand-rolled Tree-sitter structural detection before finding this. The native engine indexed 12 families from 23 artifact.json, found a shared operator across 7, and planned 6 folds at confidence 'exact-shape'.
  complement the native engine works over ARTIFACTS; the Tree-sitter pass works over SOURCE. Both are needed; neither replaces the other.
  verification_state VERIFIED_BY_MEASUREMENT

binding session:source-duplicate-census
  domain_need find structurally identical functions across the control plane
  executable_owner Tree-sitter (installed directly; bonfyre-canon advertises Tree-sitter but its extension table holds .json only)
  evidence 87 modules, 610 function bodies, 11 identical groups, 10 cross-module; largest is 15 identical ensure_schema bodies plus a second group of 6
  finding the 15/6 split IS the foreign-key split -- the 15 leave PRAGMA foreign_keys at 0, the 6 set it to 1. A single shared helper would have silently enabled constraint enforcement in 15 modules.
  scale the removal is worth ~15 lines; each body is 3 lines. The census counted copies, not code.
  verification_state VERIFIED_BY_MEASUREMENT

binding session:compression-law
  domain_need measure real compression over the estate
  executable_owner bonfyre-compress (train/pack/savings) -- but its savings report is broken
  defect raw is summed FILE bytes while compressed is a compressed TAR, so tar padding dominates; reports -58.9% on schemas/ and 0.0% on packs/ against a raw_bytes of 0
  measured_independently .yaff/.json subsets compress 3.8x (packs) and 7.7x (architecture) at zstd-19; the tool's compressed byte count matches a tar|zstd-19 reference exactly
  verification_state KNOWN_GAP

