binding session:partner-definition
  domain_need what a partner IS
  executable_owner the 41 shipped integration repos under github.com/aurekai and ~/repos -- langchain, temporal, dagster, duckdb, helm, terraform, vscode, mcp, wandb, ...
  estate_role partner_commons holds METADATA ABOUT them (176 profiles, 1,885 authored role observations); it is not the definition
  correction I treated 112 names in a markdown table as the partner surface. The shipped repos are the partner surface.
  verification_state OWNER_REUSE_REQUIRED

binding session:authored-partner-roles
  domain_need which role a method plays in which fabric, and what it must not own
  executable_owner the Gen-10 map's own tables -- '82 deep-promoted specialties' (Class, Preserved specialty, Native owner/lane, Primary paths, Pairs with) and the family tables
  evidence 146 partners carry an authored role; 72 in two or more fabrics; 32 in three or more; nine in FOUR with five distinct roles each (Qlib, vectorbt, ArcticDB, QuantLib, Formance, TigerBeetle, Hyperswitch, Interledger, Mojaloop)
  evidence 587 declared non-ownership boundaries across 104 distinct statements
  correction Pairs-with IS the compound graph I was estimating by embedding co-occurrence. Program binding is a JOIN, not a search.
  verification_state VERIFIED_BY_MEASUREMENT

binding session:method-retrieval
  domain_need given a problem, find the method
  executable_owner bonfyre-capability match / AkaiCapability
  defect advertised as semantic; scores are clean fractions of query-term overlap (0.167, 0.333). 'classify business type from a company name' misses tag-artifact, which is in the registry.
  estate_role registry wired to its own prober, 37 -> 103 capabilities; the prober's docstring names the exact defect it was written to fix
  available_fix bonfyre-embed onnx plus bonfyre-vec, used elsewhere this session, are not behind this verb
  verification_state KNOWN_GAP

