binding session:ai-leads-ranking
  domain_need rank loss-event candidates by expected realized fee
  executable_owner route_ranker.TernaryRanker plus a selective SSM over per-cell yearly sequences
  evidence 12-fold walk-forward 2015-2026: ternary+static 45.1% aggregate / 49.1% recent; real-valued weights 47.4%; real-valued + SSM 49.1% / 53.7%; oracle 83.0%
  finding ternary quantization costs 2.3 pts and the cost is WIDENING (2023 +5.1, 2025 +5.0, 2026 +9.8)
  reversal the SSM was first refused at +0.1 pts, then reversed when its own reheat condition fired the same session
  verification_state VERIFIED_BY_MEASUREMENT

binding session:ai-loss-classification
  domain_need classify the unclassified book
  executable_owner bonfyre-tag / AkaiTag (fastText) -- NOT a provider API
  evidence trained on the full 44,326-row labelled corpus (37,676 train / 6,649 held-out, 76 classes) in 16.8s; held-out 64.8% at 50,823 rows/sec; entire 8,820-name unclassified book in 155 ms at $0.00
  comparison same-size 30-row slice: fastText 83%, mistral-medium 70% at $0.001632; full book $0.00 local vs $0.48 mistral vs $6.00 opus
  correction my 30-row API benchmark was the wrong scale AND the wrong instrument
  defect bonfyre-tag's banner claims 'pure C'; it shells to Python fasttext with no startup dependency check
  verification_state VERIFIED_BY_MEASUREMENT

binding session:risk-envelope
  domain_need concentration and tail risk of what the ranker selects
  executable_owner Riskfolio-Lib -- declared role 'signal correlation/concentration/ensemble risk', must not own final decision law
  evidence ranked selection is LESS concentrated than equal weight (HHI 0.3369 vs 0.4847, 3.0 vs 2.1 effective states) but MORE volatile on every measure -- MAD 7.5x, CVaR 1.9x, MDD 1.8x
  reading the ranker diversifies WHERE it spends, not WHEN
  correction I hand-rolled an HHI before installing the partner that owns this
  verification_state VERIFIED_BY_MEASUREMENT

